From ef3a6f333f22dead576e4f52c7fdb6e835c9b462 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ssaigarimella <sgarimella34@gatech.edu>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:32:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] planner: 20 Hz control loop, margin-clean plans, PX4-feed
 staleness, escape

Fixes from the 2026-10-23 flights, each measured offline before deploying:
- ESDF slice parsed vectorized: the per-point struct.unpack loop took 1,106 ms
  per 8.7 MB outdoor slice on the Orin and starved the single-threaded node
  (control loop 2.3-4.6 Hz on every flight instead of 20). Now 48 ms; the
  rasterized grid is bit-identical (last point per cell wins, as before).
- Geofence-edge loop: A* now plans on a copy of the map with the margin band
  blocked, so a path along the fence or A*'s 1 m goal snap can no longer end
  outside the margin (delta: viewpoint (3.3,13.5) snapped to (2.3,14.4) and
  was re-planned twice a second for 23 s). Viewpoints outside the margin are
  not scored; a far out-of-margin waypoint blacklists the goal and releases
  the claim; a waypoint at the drone (takeoff on the x=0 line) is skipped as
  before; DONE when every frontier lies on/outside the margin. Replay of all
  four flights: out-of-margin plans 5->0 (delta) and 8->0 (thunderstrike),
  same goal in the other 298 frames.
- PX4 feed stale > px4_stale_s (2 s): state PX4_STALE, no setpoints at all
  (ghost 14:22: the FLU->NED offset rebuilt against a frozen NED pose anchored
  every setpoint to the freeze point; the drone oscillated in Offboard ~80 s).
  CSV gains a px4_age column.
- Escape: after 3 NO PATH with the start cell in collision, A* may snap the
  start up to escape_snap_m (2.5 m); that leg is left to the depth guard.
- Planner CSV fsync every ~5 s (power cuts zeroed every log tail).
- Lane assignment ignores radio-only peers (flag bit 7 from coordination_node).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
